; A group's targets are a *set*: the order they were listed in is not part
; of the namespace's identity.
;
; `forwards` and `backwards` list the same two forms in opposite orders, so
; they declare one namespace, twice. Keyed on the written order they were
; two namespaces over the same names, and all three consequences below were
; visible at once: the duplicate `same` was reported once per namespace,
; the `cross_ref_target_collapse` warning that tells the author their
; second `:name-key` is ignored went silent, and a `:union` over both
; warned that declaration order picks the entity when both readings picked
; the same one.
;
; What the corpus can assert is the first and the third — counts. One
; `duplicate_cross_ref_target`, and no `union_ambiguous` at the reference.
; The collapse warning is here too, which is the fix's other half: the two
; kinds disagree about `:name-key`, so exactly one of them builds the set.
(plugin :name gpu :version "1.0.0" :sjon "1.3"
  (value-kind :name forwards :underlying symbol
    :cross-ref (cross-ref :target [render-pipeline compute-pipeline]))

  (value-kind :name backwards :underlying symbol
    :cross-ref (cross-ref :target [compute-pipeline render-pipeline] :name-key alias))

  (value-kind :name either :underlying union
    :union (union-shape :alternatives [forwards backwards]))

  (form :name render-pipeline
    (key :name name  :type symbol)
    (key :name alias :type symbol))

  (form :name compute-pipeline
    (key :name name  :type symbol)
    (key :name alias :type symbol))

  (form :name dispatch
    (key :name pipeline :type either)))

(render-pipeline  :name same :alias one)
(compute-pipeline :name same :alias two)

(dispatch :pipeline same)
